From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: fix CPU-to-WiFi HNAT QDMA SG routing

CPU-to-WiFi HNAT reinjection changes the FPORT of the first QDMA
descriptor to PPE0.  mtk_tx_map() initializes every following SG
descriptor separately, however, and restores the normal GMAC FPORT on
those descriptors.  A non-linear skb is consequently submitted as one
descriptor chain with inconsistent destinations.

Remember the HNAT destination and apply it to every descriptor belonging
to the skb.  This preserves TSO/GSO and SG while keeping the complete
packet on the PPE0 path.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -1854,6 +1854,9 @@ static int mtk_tx_map(struct sk_buff *sk
 	struct mtk_tx_dma *itxd_pdma, *txd_pdma;
 	struct mtk_tx_buf *itx_buf, *tx_buf;
 	int i, n_desc = 1;
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT)
+	bool hnat_to_ppe = false;
+#endif
 	int queue = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb);
 	int k = 0;
 
@@ -1882,10 +1885,11 @@ static int mtk_tx_map(struct sk_buff *sk
 	/* TX SG offload */
 	txd = itxd;
 	txd_pdma = qdma_to_pdma(ring, txd);
-	#if defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT) || defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT_MODULE)
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT)
 	if (HNAT_SKB_CB2(skb)->magic == 0x78681415) {
-		txd->txd4 &= ~(0xf << TX_DMA_FPORT_SHIFT_V2);
-		txd->txd4 |= 0x3 << TX_DMA_FPORT_SHIFT_V2;
+		hnat_to_ppe = true;
+		txd->txd4 &= ~(TX_DMA_FPORT_MASK_V2 << TX_DMA_FPORT_SHIFT_V2);
+		txd->txd4 |= PSE_PPE0_PORT << TX_DMA_FPORT_SHIFT_V2;
 	}
 #endif
 
@@ -1921,6 +1925,16 @@ static int mtk_tx_map(struct sk_buff *sk
 
 			mtk_tx_set_dma_desc(dev, txd, &txd_info);
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT)
+			/* Keep all descriptors of this packet on the same PSE
+			 * destination. mtk_tx_set_dma_desc() otherwise restores
+			 * the normal GMAC FPORT for each SG descriptor.
+			 */
+			if (hnat_to_ppe) {
+				txd->txd4 &= ~(TX_DMA_FPORT_MASK_V2 << TX_DMA_FPORT_SHIFT_V2);
+				txd->txd4 |= PSE_PPE0_PORT << TX_DMA_FPORT_SHIFT_V2;
+			}
+#endif
 			tx_buf = mtk_desc_to_tx_buf(ring, txd,
 						    soc->tx.desc_size);
 			if (new_desc)
-- 
